    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an owner **registration date** that defaults to the server's current date when not supplied, and is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges, each in its natural place:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both acceptable on `POST /api/owners` and returned on `GET`. The generator maps it to `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` \u2014 no custom formatting needed.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) column with getter/setter, plus a `@PrePersist` hook (`defaultRegistrationDate`) that sets it to `LocalDate.now()` only when null. This keeps the defaulting rule as a small, single-responsibility unit on the entity: it applies on creation, preserves any supplied date, and never touches the value on update (where the field is left alone).\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in the SQL schema; the others are updated for parity.\n\nThe existing MapStruct `OwnerMapper` picks up the new field automatically by name in both directions, so no controller or mapper changes were required. The `@PrePersist` default runs when a new owner is inserted, and the acceptance tests confirm both the default-to-today and keep-supplied-date behaviors.",
